{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795823044,"nonce":"G9YqiaReTWZqNjnnBhEpkFfnFok=","title":"Layer composites in the direct, static, overlay and 3D paths multiply by alpha twice","message":"A layer drawn onto a transparent texture holds premultiplied colour.\n`render_with_layer_effects`, `render_static_layer_damaged`'s layer pass,\n`render_overlay_with_layer_effects` and the app's 3D layer composite blit it\nas straight colour, so translucent content is faded twice: white at half alpha\nin an opacity 0.5 layer over black reads 32, not 64, and in a layer with an\nidentity colour matrix 64, not 128.\n\nThe main window composite is not affected: it straightens its textures first.\n\nRelated: 6f7cdcd, the blend branch of the composite shader dividing straight\ncolour by alpha.","files":null}]}